            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a very taste recipe and it is easy! ! I made a few modifications. I used one cup of olive oil and next time I will reduce that to 3/4-1/2 cup. I also use kalamata greek olives rather than black olives.\r\nExcellent dish which can be used as a base for many variations."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "khallsweet"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is my family's absolutely favorite meal! I reduced the amount of olive oil to 1 cup (or even less), added a bit more basil and because I love sun-dried tomatoes and goat cheese I always pile more on to my individual serving. YUM!",
            "datePublished": "2010-08-07T06:48:50.447Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Elizabeth Lombard"
            },
            "reviewBody": "WOW! Colorful, flavorful, unique.\r\nThis is outstanding but I had to modified it for my family.\r\n My changes were; Omit olives. \r\n Reduce sundried tomatoes and canned tomatoes by at least half.\r\nAdd fresh spinach, fresh mushrooms, artichoke hearts &amp; one diced shallot, if you have it.\r\n I used goat cheese but it wasn't Feta.\r\n * * * * * *\r\n Perfect for Lenten meals and terrific dish for veggie daughter. \r\n Will put this on the \"Active List\"\r\n Thanks, Patti.",
            "datePublished": "2004-04-06T15:27:17.600Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "RiShi"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious! I received a lot of compliments. The serving size of 7 is misleading, though. I made the sauce following the recipe portions precisely, but didn't catch that the sauce is for TWO boxes of pasta until I was ready to cook the pasta. Considering that the serving size of a 16oz pasta box I had is 8, this recipe is NOT for 7 servings. I used all the juices in canned tomatoes and olives because the recipe didn't say anything about draining the liquid. (It helped cut the oiliness, I think.) I only used half the sauce for the potluck and saved the rest for another group lunch. Each batch had PLENTY for groups of 7+ people.",
            "datePublished": "2018-02-16T07:43:56.093Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "yelorz"
            },
